<div class="hero-unit">
  <h1><%== @closed == :app ? "This app needs to move" : "This service is closed to new websites" %></h1>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <div class="section narrow large">
    <% if @closed == :app %>
      <p>
        IndieAuth.com no longer signs people in for apps it has not seen before, ahead of being shut
        down. <strong><%= @app_host || 'The app that sent you here' %></strong> is not one of the apps
        already using it, so this sign-in cannot be completed.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Nothing on your own website needs to change.</strong> This is the app's to fix: its
        developer should use <a href="https://indielogin.com/api">IndieLogin.com</a>, which signs
        people in the same way and is the replacement for this part of IndieAuth.com. Passing that
        on is the most useful thing you can do.
      </p>
    <% else %>
      <p>
        IndieAuth.com is being replaced and no longer takes on websites it has not seen before.
        <% if (replacement = replacement_service) %>
          Your website can use <a href="<%= replacement.url %>"><%= replacement.name %></a> instead,
          which does the same job and signs you in with a passkey rather than a linked GitHub or
          email account.
        <% else %>
          See <a href="https://indieweb.org/IndieAuth">indieweb.org/IndieAuth</a> for the current
          options.
        <% end %>
      </p>
      <p>
        Websites already signing in through this service keep working, and will be given plenty of
        notice before it shuts down.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>

</div><!-- container -->

<%= partial :'partials/_footer' %>
